# Third-party notices

## Provider logos

`frontend/public/logos/` contains word marks and logos belonging to the model
providers this app can call — Google, OpenAI, Meta, ByteDance, Alibaba,
Tencent, Black Forest Labs, Stability AI, Ideogram, Luma, Kling, Lightricks,
Meshy, Bria, ElevenLabs, Veed, xAI and fal.ai among them.

They are used solely to identify each provider in the model picker. They are
**not** covered by this project's Apache-2.0 licence, are not the project's to
sublicense, and remain the property of their respective owners. No affiliation
with or endorsement by any of them is claimed.

If you own one of these marks and would rather it were not here, open an issue
and it will be removed.

## Runtime dependencies loaded from a CDN

The embed pages load two libraries directly from public CDNs rather than
bundling them, each pinned and integrity-checked:

- [`@google/model-viewer`](https://modelviewer.dev) 3.5.0 — the 3D and
  rigged-character viewers. The package is Apache-2.0; the built bundle also
  carries BSD-3-Clause and MIT components.
- [`A-Frame`](https://aframe.io) 1.5.0 (MIT) — the 360° panorama viewer

The Miro Web SDK is loaded from `miro.com` as Miro requires.
